rbitration</strong></h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>Not applicable to residents of Québec:&nbsp; To the extent permitted by applicable law</strong>, unless we agree otherwise, any claim, dispute or controversy, whether in contract or tort, under statute or regulation, or otherwise, and whether pre-existing, present or future, arising out of or relating to the following items will be determined by final and binding arbitration to the exclusion of the courts:</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:list -->\n<ul><li>these Terms, including, without limitation, any license granted under these Terms;</li><li>the Services or a Rogers Media Site;</li><li>oral or written statements, advertisements or promotions relating to these Terms, the Services or a Rogers Media Site; or</li><li>the relationships that result from these Terms.</li></ul>\n<!-- /wp:list -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>Not applicable to residents of Québec:&nbsp; Where applicable</strong>, arbitration will be conducted in the province in which you reside, on a simplified and expedited basis by one arbitrator under the current laws and rules relating to commercial arbitration in the province or jurisdiction in which you reside on the date of the notice. Rogers will pay all reasonable costs associated with that arbitration. Any arbitration will be conducted in accordance with our Arbitration Protocol, which is available at <a href=\"http://www.rogers.com/terms\">http://www.rogers.com/terms</a>.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:heading {\"level\":3} -->\n<h3>21. <strong>Other Important Terms</strong></h3>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>These Terms are governed exclusively by the laws of the province in which you reside, but if you reside outside of Canada, then these Terms are governed exclusively by the laws of the province of Ontario and the laws of Canada applicable therein, without giving effect to their conflict of laws principles, and you 